{"page":656,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.33117,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"642 Chapter 10: Infinite Sequences and Series"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09387,"w":0.59301,"h":0.01475,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"If \u0002 x\u0002 … 1, the right side of this inequality approaches zero as n S q. Therefore"},{"x":0.32414,"y":0.11049,"w":0.22374,"h":0.01498,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"limnSqRn(x) = 0 if \u0002 x\u0002 … 1 and"},{"x":0.55638,"y":0.13194,"w":0.0697,"h":0.01467,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"(-1)nx2n+1"},{"x":0.46587,"y":0.14127,"w":0.08585,"h":0.01815,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"tan-1x = a"},{"x":0.56679,"y":0.14247,"w":0.15875,"h":0.02068,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"2n + 1 , \u0002 x\u0002 … 1."},{"x":0.89318,"y":0.15722,"w":0.01907,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(3)"},{"x":0.53274,"y":0.15725,"w":0.02065,"h":0.00916,"fs":0.0087,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"n=0"},{"x":0.46483,"y":0.17034,"w":0.11089,"h":0.02141,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"tan-1x = x - x3"},{"x":0.56504,"y":0.17034,"w":0.23277,"h":0.02878,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"3 + x5 5 - x7 7 + g, \u0002 x\u0002 … 1."},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.20454,"w":0.59297,"h":0.04348,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"We take this route instead of finding the Taylor series directly because the formulas for the higher-order derivatives of tan-1x are unmanageable. When we put x = 1 in Equa- tion (3), we get Leibniz’s formula:"},{"x":0.44449,"y":0.25261,"w":0.2888,"h":0.03092,"fs":0.01279,"n":6,"k":0,"t":"4 = 1 - 1 3 + 1 5 - 1 7 + 1 9 - g + (-1)n"},{"x":0.69091,"y":0.26268,"w":0.10189,"h":0.02068,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"2n + 1 + g."},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.28698,"w":0.59303,"h":0.04417,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Because this series converges very slowly, it is not used in approximating p to many decimal places. The series for tan-1x converges most rapidly when x is near zero. For that reason, people who use the series for tan-1x to compute p use various trigonometric identities."},{"x":0.35276,"y":0.33371,"w":0.09992,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"For example, if"},{"x":0.49396,"y":0.35737,"w":0.07682,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"a = tan-11"},{"x":0.5626,"y":0.35737,"w":0.17322,"h":0.02703,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"2 and b = tan-11"},{"x":0.72764,"y":0.3644,"w":0.01397,"h":0.01991,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"3,"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.39509,"w":0.02817,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"then"},{"x":0.66792,"y":0.41151,"w":0.13159,"h":0.04081,"fs":0.01279,"n":6,"k":0,"t":"1 2 + 1 3 1 - 1 6 = 1 = tan p"},{"x":0.43604,"y":0.41537,"w":0.22447,"h":0.03041,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"tan (a + b) = tan a + tan b 1 - tan a tan b ="},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.45649,"w":0.02362,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"and"},{"x":0.50955,"y":0.48014,"w":0.21817,"h":0.02703,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"4 = a + b = tan-11 2 + tan-11 3."},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.50743,"w":0.59303,"h":0.03858,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Now Equation (3) may be used with x = 1>2 to evaluate tan-1(1>2) and with x = 1>3 to give tan-1(1>3). The sum of these results, multiplied by 4, gives p."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.56227,"w":0.2452,"h":0.01375,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Evaluating Indeterminate Forms"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.58693,"w":0.59294,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"We can sometimes evaluate indeterminate forms by expressing the functions involved as Taylor series."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.63126,"w":0.18183,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 5 Evaluate"},{"x":0.61011,"y":0.65517,"w":0.04555,"h":0.02721,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"ln x x - 1."},{"x":0.57991,"y":0.66238,"w":0.0239,"h":0.02013,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"lim xS1"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.6935,"w":0.59302,"h":0.04434,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Solution We represent ln x as a Taylor series in powers of x - 1. This can be accom- plished by calculating the Taylor series generated by ln x at x = 1 directly or by replacing x by x - 1 in the series for ln(1 + x) in Section 10.7, Example 6. Either way, we obtain"},{"x":0.51107,"y":0.74871,"w":0.13159,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"ln x = (x - 1) - 1"},{"x":0.63448,"y":0.75059,"w":0.11948,"h":0.02515,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"2(x - 1)2 + g,"},{"x":0.32334,"y":0.78644,"w":0.15778,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"from which we find that"},{"x":0.56902,"y":0.80669,"w":0.07733,"h":0.03057,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"xS1 a1 - 1"},{"x":0.63817,"y":0.80669,"w":0.1586,"h":0.03044,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"2(x - 1) + gb = 1."},{"x":0.50484,"y":0.80991,"w":0.087,"h":0.02721,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"ln x x - 1 = lim"},{"x":0.47464,"y":0.81713,"w":0.0239,"h":0.02013,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"lim xS1"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.85166,"w":0.54034,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Of course, this particular limit can be evaluated using l’Hôpital’s Rule just as well."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.88065,"w":0.18183,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 6 Evaluate"},{"x":0.58498,"y":0.90517,"w":0.08595,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"sin x - tan x"},{"x":0.55887,"y":0.91305,"w":0.0239,"h":0.02013,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"lim xS0"},{"x":0.62135,"y":0.91305,"w":0.05536,"h":0.02159,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"x3 ."}]}